# Craft command authoring

Product commands bootstrap a phase chat and **defer** to step instructions. They are not marathon orchestrators.

## Three layers (do not collapse)

| Layer | Path | Ends where |
|---|---|---|
| Product command | `.cursor/commands/craft-*.md` | Markdown packet loaded; follow inlined `## Instructions` |
| Step instructions | `.cursor/foundry/nodes/{node-id}/instructions.md` | `transition` requested |
| Node reference | `docs/nodes/{node-id}.md` (generated) | Authors only — not runtime steward load |

**Handoff rule:** the command stops where the step file starts. Never duplicate step content in a command.

## One-question test

Before adding a line, ask: *Would the engine already have done this before returning my context packet?*

If yes → delete it. Put lifecycle, hooks, checks, routing, and registry detail in generated node docs or engine specs instead.

## Required shape

```markdown
---
name: craft-<phase>
description: >-
  Third-person: what it does and when to use it (trigger terms).
---

# Craft <phase>

[Role: one line]

## User input
[work_prompt capture only — verbatim, no source-kind enumeration]

## Bootstrap
[cli resolve → run create or run resume → run context --markdown → follow packet]

## Out of scope
[sibling /craft-* table]
```

## Rules

1. **Bootstrap only** — `cli resolve`, then `run create` (or `run resume`), then `run context --markdown`, then stop.
2. **No environment prose** — no `**Application repo:**`, no hardcoded `.cursor/foundry/cli/...` paths, no "record `foundry_cli`" narration.
3. **No step duplication** — follow the markdown packet (`## Instructions` is inlined); pass `work_prompt` when the step says to.
4. **No lifecycle checks, next-node prep, or node-doc links.**
5. **Bootstrap failure** — manifest/bootstrap failure → foundry-app-bootstrap skill (`app discover` / `app init`); do not name catalog check ids.
6. **Bootstrap is fences only** — consecutive `foundry-invoke` fences with at most one-line failure handling.

## `foundry-invoke` fences

Foundry engine calls use `foundry-invoke` fences — **not** shell commands. Argv tail only (no `python`, no `foundry.py`, no `foundry.sh`, no `--json`).

Placeholders after context loads: `{run_id}`, `{visit_id}`, `{workspace}` from the context packet.

```foundry-invoke
run context --run "{run_id}" --markdown
```

**Shell translation:** after bootstrap, `$cli_path --json <argv>` — global `--json` comes **before** the subcommand (e.g. `$cli_path --json cli resolve`, not `$cli_path cli resolve --json`). See [steward UX](steward-ux.mdc) for bootstrap and caching `cli_path`.

Use `text` / `bash` fences only for real shell (`git`, `gh`, `dotnet`).

## Engine domain — keep out of commands

| Topic | Why |
|---|---|
| Lifecycle states and hook timing | Engine-owned |
| Catalog check probes | Engine records `check.recorded` |
| Connection selection / next node | Post-seal routing |
| `recommended_next_state` | Engine-owned after seal |
| Links to `flows/implementation/registry.yaml` or node docs | Authors only |

## Anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Fix |
|---|---|
| `**Application repo:**` / `**Foundry CLI:**` blocks | `cli resolve` + markdown packet |
| Enumerating work-prompt source kinds | "Capture verbatim" only |
| Hardcoded foundry bundle paths | `foundry-invoke` + packet placeholders |
| ` ```text ` fences for `run create` | `foundry-invoke` |
| Ticket / `source_type` in command | Step file only |
| Phase duplicating step file | Follow inlined `## Instructions` |
| `run context --json` then read `instructions_path` | `run context --markdown` (instructions inlined) |
